          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: Successive observations made between June 7, 1999, and the end of August 1999. The witness reported in 2008 observations of light phenomena moving in the night sky. Only one testimony was collected. This testimony is not exploitable by GEIPAN because it consists of a series of distinct observations reported 10 years after the facts without specifying the exact dates of each. As a result, the observations are multiple, disparate, and imprecise. They do not appear to be incompatible with observations of satellites, meteors (especially in August), or even stars. Consequently, GEIPAN classifies this case as C: lack of information.",
